# ⌘L with the Library open in the floating sidebar (11 Nov 2026): the Library slides back to the space
# the way its ← and Escape do, the floating sidebar staying out, and the address opens on the
# sidebar's field (the bar is open, unseen, meanwhile, so typing isn't lost). Before, the drawer was
# cut off at the sidebar's width and the tab list came back in one jump.
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
wait 1.5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=address
wait 2
cra://action/toggleSidebar
wait 1
cra://debug?floatingSidebar=1
wait 1
cra://action/openLibrary
wait 1.5
cra://action/editURL
expect-log command bar waits for the Library to slide back
expect-log command bar opens on the address after the Library \(on its field\)
reject-log library closes directly
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarState=address
expect-log command bar address: open=1 dropdown=1
cra://debug?closeCommandBar=1
wait 0.5
